WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.909
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online C two, Book two.

2
00:00:05.209 --> 00:00:08.897
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.197 --> 00:00:15.785
Unit nineteen: Critical Theory. Today you will link ideas to action using aim/goal infinitive clauses.

4
00:00:16.085 --> 00:00:18.831
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.767 --> 00:00:23.487
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:25.653
Critical theory.

7
00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:31.738
Critical theory means social analysis that aims to expose and change structures of domination.

8
00:00:32.350 --> 00:00:36.079
Critical theory examines whom a social arrangement truly serves.

9
00:00:36.683 --> 00:00:39.742
Your turn. Say: Critical theory.

10
00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:43.764
Critical theory.

11
00:00:44.517 --> 00:00:45.762
Power structure.

12
00:00:46.750 --> 00:00:50.909
Power structure means the arrangement of who holds influence and who does not.

13
00:00:51.517 --> 00:00:54.921
The power structure of the firm favoured senior male managers.

14
00:00:55.517 --> 00:00:58.587
Your turn. Say: Power structure.

15
00:01:01.433 --> 00:01:02.818
Power structure.

16
00:01:03.583 --> 00:01:04.886
Emancipation.

17
00:01:05.883 --> 00:01:10.019
Emancipation means liberation from oppression or restrictive constraints.

18
00:01:10.617 --> 00:01:14.892
Emancipation requires changing conditions, not only attitudes.

19
00:01:15.483 --> 00:01:18.565
Your turn. Say: Emancipation.

20
00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:22.610
Emancipation.

21
00:01:23.350 --> 00:01:25.013
Ideology critique.

22
00:01:26.017 --> 00:01:31.360
Ideology critique means analysis of how beliefs conceal and justify unequal power.

23
00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:35.819
Ideology critique asks who benefits from a 'common sense' belief.

24
00:01:36.417 --> 00:01:39.824
Your turn. Say: Ideology critique.

25
00:01:42.667 --> 00:01:44.829
Ideology critique.

26
00:01:45.583 --> 00:01:46.457
Hegemony.

27
00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:51.551
Hegemony means dominance maintained through consent as much as force.

28
00:01:52.150 --> 00:01:55.879
Hegemony works when the powerless accept the rules as natural.

29
00:01:56.483 --> 00:01:59.182
Your turn. Say: Hegemony.

30
00:02:02.033 --> 00:02:03.139
Hegemony.

31
00:02:03.883 --> 00:02:05.326
Social justice.

32
00:02:06.317 --> 00:02:11.718
Social justice means fairness in the distribution of rights, opportunities and resources.

33
00:02:12.317 --> 00:02:15.315
Social justice is the goal of many reform movements.

34
00:02:15.917 --> 00:02:18.766
Your turn. Say: Social justice.

35
00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:23.240
Social justice.

36
00:02:23.983 --> 00:02:25.031
Praxis.

37
00:02:26.017 --> 00:02:29.212
Praxis means the unity of theory and practical action.

38
00:02:29.817 --> 00:02:32.966
For critical theorists, praxis is the test of an idea.

39
00:02:33.550 --> 00:02:35.993
Your turn. Say: Praxis.

40
00:02:38.833 --> 00:02:39.811
Praxis.

41
00:02:40.550 --> 00:02:41.609
Liberation.

42
00:02:42.617 --> 00:02:45.858
Liberation means the act of being set free from constraint.

43
00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:49.390
Liberation was both the movement's aim and its method.

44
00:02:49.983 --> 00:02:52.403
Your turn. Say: Liberation.

45
00:02:55.267 --> 00:02:56.419
Liberation.

46
00:02:57.233 --> 00:03:01.140
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:03:01.983 --> 00:03:07.480
Visal, philosophers write about oppression, yet little seems to change. What is the point?

48
00:03:08.583 --> 00:03:17.772
Critical theory aims to connect ideas with real action. Its goal is not merely to interpret society but to change it.

49
00:03:18.883 --> 00:03:20.070
Change how?

50
00:03:21.183 --> 00:03:32.288
By exposing the beliefs that make inequality seem natural. The aim of ideology critique is to reveal who profits from a supposedly neutral rule.

51
00:03:33.383 --> 00:03:34.326
And then?

52
00:03:35.417 --> 00:03:45.824
Praxis. The purpose of theory is to inform action, and the purpose of action is to test theory, in a continuing cycle.

53
00:03:46.967 --> 00:03:48.560
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:49.417 --> 00:03:52.995
Grammar focus: Aim and goal infinitive clauses.

55
00:03:53.295 --> 00:03:54.552
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:55.250 --> 00:03:58.329
Critical theory aims to connect ideas with real action.

57
00:03:59.217 --> 00:04:02.946
Ideology critique seeks to reveal who profits from a rule.

58
00:04:03.850 --> 00:04:06.767
The goal of praxis is to unite theory and practice.

59
00:04:07.733 --> 00:04:17.932
Aim, seek, strive, intend and be designed take 'to' + base verb: aims to connect. 'The aim of X is to…' also needs the infinitive, never '-ing' after 'aims'.

60
00:04:18.683 --> 00:04:23.193
Be careful! Don't say: Critical theory aims connecting ideas to action.

61
00:04:25.133 --> 00:04:28.375
Say: Critical theory aims to connect ideas to action.

62
00:04:28.675 --> 00:04:30.280
aim + to-infinitive.

63
00:04:31.067 --> 00:04:33.823
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:34.633 --> 00:04:36.180
Theory With a Purpose.

65
00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:46.061
The Frankfurt School, founded in the 1920s, developed critical theory to analyse how capitalism, culture and ideology maintain unequal power.

66
00:04:47.067 --> 00:04:55.777
Unlike traditional theory, which aims to describe the world neutrally, critical theory seeks to expose domination and to promote emancipation.

67
00:04:56.767 --> 00:05:04.978
Antonio Gramsci's notion of hegemony explained how rulers secure consent, so that unequal arrangements appear to be natural common sense.

68
00:05:05.967 --> 00:05:10.637
The method of ideology critique is designed to reveal whose interests a belief serves.

69
00:05:11.633 --> 00:05:18.962
Praxis, the union of reflection and action, completes the project: ideas are tested by their capacity to bring about liberation.

70
00:05:20.067 --> 00:05:24.231
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:05:25.083 --> 00:05:28.395
Critical theory aims blank connect ideas with action.

72
00:05:28.695 --> 00:05:31.861
A, to. B, for. C, at.

73
00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:37.249
The answer is A: to.

74
00:05:38.383 --> 00:05:41.242
The unity of theory and practical action is blank.

75
00:05:41.542 --> 00:05:45.671
A, hegemony. B, praxis. C, emancipation.

76
00:05:49.233 --> 00:05:51.198
The answer is B: praxis.

77
00:05:52.350 --> 00:05:54.686
Dominance maintained through consent is blank.

78
00:05:54.986 --> 00:05:59.174
A, hegemony. B, liberation. C, social justice.

79
00:06:02.733 --> 00:06:04.686
The answer is A: hegemony.

80
00:06:05.850 --> 00:06:07.629
Choose the correct sentence.

81
00:06:07.929 --> 00:06:16.145
A, The theory aims exposing power.. B, The theory aims to expose power.. C, The theory aims for expose power..

82
00:06:19.700 --> 00:06:22.988
The answer is B: The theory aims to expose power..

83
00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:28.808
According to the reading, critical theory differs from traditional theory because it seeks to…

84
00:06:29.108 --> 00:06:34.933
A, describe neutrally. B, expose domination. C, avoid action.

85
00:06:38.467 --> 00:06:40.849
The answer is B: expose domination.

86
00:06:42.033 --> 00:06:45.266
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:06:46.117 --> 00:06:50.485
How does critical theory connect abstract ideas to real-world action?

88
00:07:07.283 --> 00:07:08.702
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:07:09.002 --> 00:07:37.167
Critical theory connects ideas to action by revealing the hidden assumptions that keep unfair arrangements in place. Once people see that a rule benefits some at the expense of others, change becomes thinkable. The aim is not only to understand society but to transform it. Praxis closes the loop: ideas guide action, and the results of action test the ideas.

90
00:07:37.467 --> 00:07:39.188
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:07:40.083 --> 00:07:45.011
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and aim and goal infinitive clauses.

92
00:07:45.311 --> 00:07:50.576
Today's value is social justice. Work for a world where everyone is treated fairly.

93
00:07:50.876 --> 00:07:53.563
See you in Unit twenty. Goodbye!

94
00:07:53.863 --> 00:07:57.096
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

